Upstream splits its licence per directory and says so in LICENSING.md. The
skill surface, skills/, is MIT and is the only part copied here. The
compression engine and the Go binaries that embed it -- engine/, proxy/,
rewriter/, browse/, mcp/, shrink/, the cavemem Go core and shared/platform/ --
are Business Source License 1.1, which requires a commercial licence to offer
the functionality to third parties as a hosted or embedded service.

None of that is vendored. This repository takes the one file that owns response
style and nothing that is engine-linked, so no BSL-1.1 obligation attaches.

Only SKILL.md is copied. Upstream's own commands, plugin manifest and Go
tooling are not, so `/caveman` here is a skill invocation rather than the
upstream slash command.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Copies are byte-for-byte. They are not edited to fit this repository's house
style: a vendored file that quietly diverges from upstream is harder to trust
than one that is either identical or openly forked. Check for drift with:

    bash scripts/check-vendor-drift.sh
